From af9dfcd8771853f721212e07abae578df556c52f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HR_Z <2463882771@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:08:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] Report which DxeCore insert site handed InsertTailList
 a bad list head

DxeCore asserts on every boot with:

  ASSERT [DxeCore] .../LinkedList.c(267): InternalBaseLibIsListValid (ListHead)

which is InsertTailList refusing a LIST_ENTRY that is not a valid initialised
list. BaseLib cannot say which call site did it - it has no DebugLib dependency
and adding one would be a library cycle - so the assert names the expression and
nothing more. DxeCore has around twenty insert sites and each means something
different, so the message alone is not actionable.

CORE_INSERT_TAIL wraps the insert with a check and prints only when the head is
bad, with the file, line, and the head's own links. Every InsertTailList call in
Core/Dxe now goes through it.

Misc/MemoryProtectionSupport.c did not include DxeMain.h and now does.

This is diagnostic scaffolding for a bring-up problem, not a fix: the assert
itself is still there and still fires. Once the offending site is known it can be
replaced with a real fix and this can be removed.

Co-Authored-By: WorkBuddy <noreply@workbuddy.ai>
